                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "620be645-b082-362d-8ed0-3ed731a1d581",
                        "entry_id": "1bb4cda2-756a-357d-891a-3e4cf52533bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A thief who steals livestock in large quantities."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d1d6c2b-3c10-4db9-9343-3c6da649433a",
                                "sense_id": "620be645-b082-362d-8ed0-3ed731a1d581",
                                "text": "In the Civil Law, he was accounted an Abigeus who carried off one Horse or one Ox, or four Swine or ten Sheep; if he took a smaller Number of Swine or Sheep, he was reckoned a Fur rather than an Abigeus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bb9196e-5a32-424f-8a04-573e4efb88e0",
                                "sense_id": "620be645-b082-362d-8ed0-3ed731a1d581",
                                "text": "The stealing of a single horse or ox might make a man an abigeus, but it seems that the crime could not be committed on less than four pigs or ten sheep."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b743247-ad7d-4b3c-b24f-59d6893b5452",
                                "sense_id": "620be645-b082-362d-8ed0-3ed731a1d581",
                                "text": "It is obvious why the thief of only one domestic animal was not treated so severely as an abigeus. The reason for the severe punishment of rustlers, abigei, was the need of a stronger protection for agricultural interest, particularly in countries where these offenses were more frequent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
